    "englishSummary": "Sir Syed explains that Islam replaced nationhood based on race or land with a spiritual brotherhood founded on the Kalima, yet Muslims now live like the brothers of Joseph, divided by envy and minor disputes. Unity does not require one creed: belief is between a person and God, while love, help and sympathy are owed to fellow human beings, including non-Muslim countrymen in civic life. All progress comes from unity; working for national unity is a greater virtue than other good works.",
