    "englishSummary": "On a stormy night the ailing Dr Zaidi keeps hearing a knock at the door; his wife insists it is the wind and his imagination. Young Dr Burhan arrives to treat him, and Zaidi confesses that eighteen or twenty years earlier he refused, out of tiredness, to go with an old man whose son was gravely ill, while the man knocked at his door for a long time. Burhan says the knock is Zaidi's conscience, then reveals that he is that old man's grandson, whose father died that night, yet he has cared for Zaidi faithfully.",
