    "englishSummary": "The doctor says the overworked Mr Ashfaq needs no medicine, only rest, quiet and no noise in his room. His wife promises silence but immediately chatters, scolds the servant Lallu and the water-carrier, hunts for the bell and argues about food; then come the child's rattling toy car and crying, the sweeper's dust, a telephone call, the neighbour's tuneless harmonium, a beggar and Lallu pounding soapnuts. At last the exhausted husband asks for his cap and sherwani: he is going to the office \"for rest and quiet\".",
