    "englishSummary": "Colonel Muhammad Khan's humorous essay begins with his principled friend Agha, who \"invites\" him to a robbery to make him see that his own recommendation for a clerk was robbery: taking someone else's right. The author then sketches recommendation-seekers: the uncle's note asking him to free a black-marketeer from an honest officer, the over-familiar blackmailer who says \"Pakistan is in God's hands\", and the maulana who quotes Iqbal to sell ten thousand copies of a worthless book. Krishan Chander's false promises ended in disaster; the only remedy is to treat a recommendation-seeker as a thief.",
